<section>
  <exercises>
    <heading level="1">Section 4.5 Exercises</heading>
    <heading level="1">Practice Makes Perfect</heading>
    <paragraph>Write the Augmented Matrix for a System of Equations</paragraph>
    <paragraph>In the following exercises, write each system of linear equations as an augmented matrix.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="196" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$\left\{ \begin{array}{l} {3x - y = -1} \\ {2y = 2x + 5} \end{array} \right.$$ ⓑ $$\left\{ \begin{array}{l} {4x + 3y = -2} \\ {x - 2y - 3z = 7} \\ {2x - y + 2z = -6} \end{array} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="197" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$\left\{ \begin{array}{l} {2x + 4y = -5} \\ {3x - 2y = 2} \end{array} \right.$$ ⓑ $$\left\{ \begin{array}{l} {3x - 2y - z = -2} \\ {-2x + y = 5} \\ {5x + 4y + z = -1} \end{array} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$[24-53-22][24-53-22]$$ ⓑ $$[3-2-1-2-2105541-1][3-2-1-2-2105541-1]$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="198" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$\left\{ \begin{array}{l} {3x - y = -4} \\ {2x = y + 2} \end{array} \right.$$ ⓑ $$\left\{ \begin{array}{l} {x - 3y - 4z = -2} \\ {4x + 2y + 2z = 5} \\ {2x - 5y + 7z = -8} \end{array} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="199" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$\left\{ \begin{array}{l} {2x - 5y = -3} \\ {4x = 3y - 1} \end{array} \right.$$ ⓑ $$\left\{ \begin{matrix} {4x + 3y - 2z = -3} \\ {-2x + y - 3z = 4} \\ {-x - 4y + 5z = -2} \end{matrix} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$[2-5-34-3-1][2-5-34-3-1]$$ ⓑ $$[43-2-3-21-34-1-45-2][43-2-3-21-34-1-45-2]$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>Write the system of equations that corresponds to the augmented matrix.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="200" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\lbrack {\left. \begin{array}{lccr} 2 &amp; &amp; &amp; -1 \\ 1 &amp; &amp; &amp; -3 \end{array} \right|} \right.\left. \begin{array}{r} 4 \\ 2 \end{array} \right\rbrack$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="201" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\lbrack {\left. \begin{array}{lccr} 2 &amp; &amp; &amp; -4 \\ 3 &amp; &amp; &amp; -3 \end{array} \right|} \right.\left. \begin{array}{r} -2 \\ -1 \end{array} \right\rbrack$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$${ 2 x - 4 y = -2 3 x - 3 y = -1 { 2 x - 4 y = -2 3 x - 3 y = -1$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="202" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\lbrack {\left. \begin{array}{lccrccr} 1 &amp; &amp; &amp; 0 &amp; &amp; &amp; -3 \\ 1 &amp; &amp; &amp; -2 &amp; &amp; &amp; 0 \\ 0 &amp; &amp; &amp; -1 &amp; &amp; &amp; 2 \end{array} \right|} \right.\left. \begin{array}{r} -1 \\ -2 \\ 3 \end{array} \right\rbrack$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="203" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\lbrack {\left. \begin{array}{lccrccr} 2 &amp; &amp; &amp; -2 &amp; &amp; &amp; 0 \\ 0 &amp; &amp; &amp; 2 &amp; &amp; &amp; -1 \\ 3 &amp; &amp; &amp; 0 &amp; &amp; &amp; -1 \end{array} \right|} \right.\left. \begin{array}{r} -1 \\ 2 \\ -2 \end{array} \right\rbrack$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$${ 2 x - 2 y = -1 2 y - z = 2 3 x - z = -2 { 2 x - 2 y = -1 2 y - z = 2 3 x - z = -2$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>Use Row Operations on a Matrix</paragraph>
    <paragraph>In the following exercises, perform the indicated operations on the augmented matrices.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="204" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\lbrack {\left. \begin{array}{lccr} 6 &amp; &amp; &amp; -4 \\ 3 &amp; &amp; &amp; -2 \end{array} \right|} \right.\left. \begin{array}{r} 3 \\ 1 \end{array} \right\rbrack$$</paragraph>
        <paragraph>ⓐ Interchange rows 1 and 2</paragraph>
        <paragraph>ⓑ Multiply row 2 by 3</paragraph>
        <paragraph>ⓒ Multiply row 2 by $$-2$$ and add row 1 to it.</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="205" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\lbrack \left. \begin{array}{lccr} 4 &amp; &amp; &amp; -6 \\ 3 &amp; &amp; &amp; 2 \end{array} \right| \right.\left. \begin{array}{r} -3 \\ 1 \end{array} \right\rbrack$$</paragraph>
        <paragraph>ⓐ Interchange rows 1 and 2</paragraph>
        <paragraph>ⓑ Multiply row 1 by 4</paragraph>
        <paragraph>ⓒ Multiply row 2 by 3 and add row 1 to it.</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$[3214-6-3][3214-6-3]$$ ⓑ $$[12844-6-3][12844-6-3]$$ ⓒ $$[128424-10-5][128424-10-5]$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="206" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\lbrack {\left. \begin{array}{lccrccr} 4 &amp; &amp; &amp; -12 &amp; &amp; &amp; -8 \\ 4 &amp; &amp; &amp; -2 &amp; &amp; &amp; -3 \\ -6 &amp; &amp; &amp; 2 &amp; &amp; &amp; -1 \end{array} \right|} \right.\left. \begin{array}{r} 16 \\ -1 \\ -1 \end{array} \right\rbrack$$</paragraph>
        <paragraph>ⓐ Interchange rows 2 and 3</paragraph>
        <paragraph>ⓑ Multiply row 1 by 4</paragraph>
        <paragraph>ⓒ Multiply row 2 by $$-2$$ and add to row 3.</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="207" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\lbrack {\left. \begin{array}{lccrccr} 6 &amp; &amp; &amp; -5 &amp; &amp; &amp; 2 \\ 2 &amp; &amp; &amp; 1 &amp; &amp; &amp; -4 \\ 3 &amp; &amp; &amp; -3 &amp; &amp; &amp; 1 \end{array} \right|} \right.\left. \begin{array}{r} 3 \\ 5 \\ -1 \end{array} \right\rbrack$$</paragraph>
        <paragraph>ⓐ Interchange rows 2 and 3</paragraph>
        <paragraph>ⓑ Multiply row 2 by 5</paragraph>
        <paragraph>ⓒ Multiply row 3 by $$-2$$ and add to row 1.</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$6-5233-31-121-456-5233-31-121-45$$ ⓑ $$6-52315-155-521-456-52315-155-521-45$$ ⓒ $$2-710-715-155-521-452-710-715-155-521-45$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="208" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Perform the needed row operation that will get the first entry in row 2 to be zero in the augmented matrix: $$\left\lbrack {\left. \begin{array}{rccr} 1 &amp; &amp; &amp; 2 \\ -3 &amp; &amp; &amp; -4 \end{array} \right|} \right.\left. \begin{array}{r} 5 \\ -1 \end{array} \right\rbrack.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="209" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Perform the needed row operations that will get the first entry in both row 2 and row 3 to be zero in the augmented matrix: $$\left\lbrack {\left. \begin{array}{lccrccr} 1 &amp; &amp; &amp; -2 &amp; &amp; &amp; 3 \\ 3 &amp; &amp; &amp; -1 &amp; &amp; &amp; -2 \\ 2 &amp; &amp; &amp; -3 &amp; &amp; &amp; -4 \end{array} \right|} \right.\left. \begin{array}{r} -4 \\ 5 \\ -1 \end{array} \right\rbrack.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$[ 1 -2 3 -4 0 5 -11 17 0 1 -10 7 ] [ 1 -2 3 -4 0 5 -11 17 0 1 -10 7 ]$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>Solve Systems of Equations Using Matrices</paragraph>
    <paragraph>In the following exercises, solve each system of equations using a matrix.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="210" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{array}{l} {2x + y = 2} \\ {x - y = -2} \end{array} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="211" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{array}{l} {3x + y = 2} \\ {x - y = 2} \end{array} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$( 1 , -1 ) ( 1 , -1 )$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="212" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{matrix} {-x + 2y = -2} \\ {x + y = -4} \end{matrix} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="213" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{matrix} {-2x + 3y = 3} \\ {x + 3y = 12} \end{matrix} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$( 3 , 3 ) ( 3 , 3 )$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>In the following exercises, solve each system of equations using a matrix.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="214" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{matrix} {2x - 3y + z = 19} \\ {-3x + y - 2z = -15} \\ {x + y + z = 0} \end{matrix} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="215" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{matrix} {2x - y + 3z = -3} \\ {-x + 2y - z = 10} \\ {x + y + z = 5} \end{matrix} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$( -2 , 5 , 2 ) ( -2 , 5 , 2 )$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="216" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{array}{l} {2x - 6y + z = 3} \\ {3x + 2y - 3z = 2} \\ {2x + 3y - 2z = 3} \end{array} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="217" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{array}{l} {4x - 3y + z = 7} \\ {2x - 5y - 4z = 3} \\ {3x - 2y - 2z = -7} \end{array} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$( -3 , -5 , 4 ) ( -3 , -5 , 4 )$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="218" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{array}{l} {x + 2z = 0} \\ {4y + 3z = -2} \\ {2x - 5y = 3} \end{array} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="219" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{array}{l} {2x + 5y = 4} \\ {3y - z = 3} \\ {4x + 3z = -3} \end{array} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$( -3 , 2 , 3 ) ( -3 , 2 , 3 )$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="220" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{array}{l} {2y + 3z = -1} \\ {5x + 3y = -6} \\ {7x + z = 1} \end{array} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="221" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{array}{l} {3x - z = -3} \\ {5y + 2z = -6} \\ {4x + 3y = -8} \end{array} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$( -2 , 0 , -3 ) ( -2 , 0 , -3 )$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="222" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{array}{l} {2x + 3y + z = 12} \\ {x + y + z = 9} \\ {3x + 4y + 2z = 20} \end{array} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="223" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{matrix} {x + 2y + 6z = 5} \\ {-x + y - 2z = 3} \\ {x - 4y - 2z = 1} \end{matrix} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>no solution</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="224" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{array}{l} {x + 2y - 3z = -1} \\ {x - 3y + z = 1} \\ {2x - y - 2z = 2} \end{array} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="225" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{matrix} {4x - 3y + 2z = 0} \\ {-2x + 3y - 7z = 1} \\ {2x - 2y + 3z = 6} \end{matrix} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>no solution</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="226" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{matrix} {x - y + 2z = -4} \\ {2x + y + 3z = 2} \\ {-3x + 3y - 6z = 12} \end{matrix} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="227" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{matrix} {-x - 3y + 2z = 14} \\ {-x + 2y - 3z = -4} \\ {3x + y - 2z = 6} \end{matrix} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$8 5 , - 42 5 , - 24 5 8 5 , - 42 5 , - 24 5$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="228" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{matrix} {x + y - 3z = -1} \\ {y - z = 0} \\ {-x + 2y = 1} \end{matrix} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="229" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{matrix} {x + 2y + z = 4} \\ {x + y - 2z = 3} \\ {-2x - 3y + z = -7} \end{matrix} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>infinitely many solutions $$(x,y,z)(x,y,z)$$ where $$x=5z+2;y=-3z+1;zx=5z+2;y=-3z+1;z$$ is any real number</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <heading level="1">Writing Exercises</heading>
    <exercise number="230" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Solve the system of equations $$\left\{ \begin{array}{l} {x + y = 10} \\ {x - y = 6} \end{array} \right.$$ ⓐ by graphing and ⓑ by substitution. ⓒ Which method do you prefer? Why?</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="231" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Solve the system of equations $$\left\{ \begin{array}{l} {3x + y = 12} \\ {x = y - 8} \end{array} \right.$$ by substitution and explain all your steps in words.</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>Answers will vary.</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
